519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788317556152213001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"282aa9e8-baa7-4db2-98a2-f638c34530cb","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F5 (reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md), HIGH, ALREADY DRIFTED.\nDistinct from the MCP-tool-vs-facade parity gate (ticket 8ce5-b870-601d-4715): this is\nmodels-vs-schemas.\n\nsrc/rebar/_mcp_models.py:1-24 declares itself a pydantic-only leaf with no rebar.* edges, so every\nenum must be hand-copied:\n- :61-68 PinStatus (6) vs llm/plan_review/pin_health.py:21\n- :54 TargetPinStatus (4) vs pin_health.py:29 (third copy as dict keys at :193)\n- :122 FileImpactScope vs types.py:22\n- :284-295, :298, :336 vs schemas/bridge_{run,status,access_check}.schema.json\n\nTwo gaps in schemas/check_mcp_models.py:\n1. missing_declarations (:51-57) is a PROPERTY-NAME set difference; it never reads `enum`.\n2. MODEL_SCHEMAS (:22-34) covers 11 of 34 *Out models. Running the gate predicate over the\n   unregistered ones: TicketStateOut missing 23 properties, NextBatchOut 11, GateResultOut 5,\n   CreateResultOut 1. Both PlanReviewHealth*Out (carrying the pin_status copies) absent entirely.\n\nThis is the published MCP wire contract.\n\nProposed fix: add-parity-check — compare enum values, and derive/assert MODEL_SCHEMAS completeness\ninstead of hand-listing it.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"62eb-5e6f-512a-420d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP output models re-type canonical enums and the drift gate is enum-blind (mirror F5)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["35fe7266-cad6-48e8-98dd-4c056d54090d","282aa9e8-baa7-4db2-98a2-f638c34530cb","dfcd8038-8c9f-427a-abc5-c9f8b5e1b226"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788328061918392001,"uuid":"d1eaa256-8776-472b-930c-c96c15704274"}